<ArticleLayout
  title="Cortisol+ on Perplexity: Apps, HRV & Stress Questions"
  description="Explore shared Perplexity conversations on tracking cortisol, home testing, natural stress habits and wearable apps, with disclosed prompts and original sources."
  published="2026-09-13"
  updated="2026-09-16"
>
  <p>Looking into a cortisol-tracking app can raise several different questions: what the app actually measures, how it compares with alternatives, and how to use the readings in everyday life. These conversations explore those questions from different angles, including tracking cortisol at home and managing everyday stress.</p>
  <p><strong>How these answers were created:</strong> the Cortisol+ team created these conversations on September 13 and 16, 2026. The four September 16 questions started without a brand mention; none of those initial answers mentioned Cortisol+. We then explicitly introduced the app in disclosed follow-ups. The older four conversations named the app from the start. These are AI-generated answers we requested, not independent reviews, customer testimonials or an endorsement by Perplexity. Open each conversation to inspect the response and its sources.</p>
  <nav aria-label="Perplexity conversation topics">
    <ul>{conversations.map((item) => <li><a href={`#${item.id}`}>{item.title}</a></li>)}</ul>
  </nav>

  {conversations.map((item) => (
    <section aria-labelledby={item.id} class="border-t border-[color:var(--color-border)] pt-6 mt-8">
      <h2 id={item.id} class="scroll-mt-24">{item.title}</h2>
      <p>{item.description}</p>
      <p><a href={item.url}>Read “{item.title}” on Perplexity →</a></p>
      <details class="rounded-xl border border-[color:var(--color-border)] p-4 my-5">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium">See the question we asked</summary>
        <p class="break-words">{item.question}</p>
      </details>
      <p>{item.note}</p>
      <p><a href={item.guide}>{item.guideLabel} →</a></p>
    </section>
  ))}

  <h2>Read the sources alongside the answers</h2>
  <p>AI answers can contain errors or reflect older product information. The calibration correction in the “What is Cortisol+?” conversation is one example. Features, subscription terms and privacy policies can also change. Follow the cited sources and use our <a href="/how-it-works/">current methodology</a> for Cortisol+'s scoring rules.</p>
  <p>Cortisol+ organizes permitted wearable signals into a wellness score. It does not measure cortisol in blood, saliva or urine. For setup and data limitations, see the <a href="/stress/apple-watch/">Apple Watch stress guide and app walkthrough</a>.</p>
</ArticleLayout>
